<title>USA: Daxor announces annual earnings.</title>
<headline>Daxor announces annual earnings.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996		  1995</p>
<p>Total Revenues		     $ 2,865,835	 $ 4,748,935</p>
<p>Net Income (loss)		  $  (112,165)	$ 1,287,115</p>
<p>Weighted Average</p>
<p>Number of Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding			  4,722,709	   4,872,481</p>
<p>Net Income or (loss)</p>
<p>per Common Equivalent</p>
<p>  Share				$     (0.02)	$	0.26</p>
<p>Note:  Total revenues and income was decreased in 1996 because of partial closure of Daxor's facilities.  On May 30, 1996, the New York Appellate Court in a unanimous 5-0 decision ordered the full reopening of Daxor Sperm and Blood Banking facilities. Daxor currently has a Rico/Antitrust suit pending against the New York Blood Center and certain New York State Health Department officials.</p>
</text>
